+#if defined(RASPINET)
+            //
+            // The network of the Raspberry Pi as the network setup of NT 3.5 installs
+            // it: NTLANMAN.INF with OEMNADBC.INF for the Ethernet controller of the board
+            // (the Bcmeth miniport, adapter Bcmeth1), OEMNXPTC.INF for TCP/IP with DHCP
+            // and NetBIOS over TCP/IP, and the services of LAN Manager, NetBIOS and RPC,
+            // bound as the network control panel binds them. It is the registry of a
+            // developer network install (setup /i NTIDWNET.INF on the ARMNETIDW hives)
+            // without what DHCP writes while it runs, and without the Route values of
+            // the bindings (with the LanaNum and EnumExport values NBINFO.INF keeps for
+            // its routes): their strings hold quotes, which REGINI cannot write. The
+            // network control panel stores the bindings again with them when the
+            // developer first run starts NCPABIND.INF (registry.ini). The workgroup and
+            // the account domain of a developer install come from registry.ini.
+            //
+
